00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  with our lifestyle nowadays a lot of us  do suffer from lower back pain our  bodies function at their best when our  muscles work in sync with one another  weak muscles especially around the core  and pelvis can lead to back pain and any  unwanted injuries so if you do suffer  from back pain I'm good to share with  you the do's and don'ts when it comes to  movements and exercising these exercises  will have to strengthen your lower back  to prevent any unwanted injuries and for  you to lead a healthier life  avoid situps many might think that  sit-ups can strengthen the core or apps  but more often people tend to use  muscles in their hips instead of their  abs when you sit all the way up you're  lifting your tailbone off the floor and  this movement can actually cause more  pressure on the spine which can lead to  injury and pain on the lower back so if  you have a lower back pain or injury you  should definitely avoid this exercise  perform partial crunches instead partial  crunches are more effective at isolating  your abdominal muscles and prevent  excessive back stress when you crunch up  tighten your abs and only rise to where  your shoulder blades come off the mat  don't use your arms to pull your neck  off the floor your hands should gently  support your head hold for a second  right at the top then lower back down  your feet tailbone and lower back should  remain in contact with the mat  throughout  avoid double leg raises double leg  raises can help to strengthen your core  but it can put a lot of pressure on your  lower back especially if you do it wrong  or if you already do suffer from pain  this exercise should be avoided for  those with weak core or lower back by  lifting the tailbone off the floor and  arching the lower back it can create  discomfort thus making your pain worse  take it slow and perform knee to chest  instead instead of lifting both legs  together lift one at a time lie on the  mat with both legs stretched out then  bring one knee close to the chest  keeping the other leg on the floor then  lower the leg and repeat on the opposite  leg remember to keep your back flat on  the floor throughout the workout and do  not lift your tailbone off the floor  this workout strengthens the lower  abdominal without putting excess  pressure on the lower back next avoid  Superman Superman is actually a really  great workout to strengthen the lower  back muscles however if you're someone  who suffers from existing injury or  extreme pain avoid this exercise without  a strong core you might struggle to lift  both of the arms and legs off the floor  simultaneously this can cause you to  compensate on proper form and recruit  the wrong muscles when performing of  exercise some might even over arch your  lower back and jerk as they come up  which can create high amounts of stress  and discomfort to their lower back  perform birth talk of bridging instead  birth dock is a great exercise to  strengthen and stabilize of the lower  back and core without overloading the  spine start on all fours keep your back  flat and tighten your stomach muscles in  a slow and controlled manner lift and  extend one leg behind you and the  opposite arm hold for one count slowly  lower back down and switch to the  opposite side  be careful not to let your lower back  sag and dip your hips only rise to the  height where the lower back position can  be maintained or perform bridging lie on  your back with your knees bent and arms  by your sides push a huge into the floor  squeeze the glutes and lift your hips  off the floor unto the shoulders hips  and knees are in a straight line hold  for about two to three counts then  slowly lower the hips and repeat this  exercise strengthens the lower back hip  flexors and also glutes to help  stabilize the spine and to give you  proper posture avoid standing toe  touches most of us still think that  touching that toes is the best way to  stretch at their hamstrings and improve  flexibility but the truth is they may be  putting even greater stress on the discs  and ligaments in their spine toe touches  from a standing position can aggravate  pain and some might even over stretch at  the hamstrings and lower back muscles  perform hamstring stretches instead  tight hamstring muscles are one of the  most common contributors to lower back  pain the hamstring muscles run through  the back of each thigh from the hip down  to the back of the knee so to relieve  lower back pain perform hamstring  stretches regularly over time this will  lengthen and reduce tension in the  hamstring muscles hence reducing stress  felt in the lower back lie flat on your  back with your knees bent look at our  around the calf of one foot straighten  your knee and slowly draw your leg  towards you you should feel a gentle  stretch down the back of your leg don't  force at the stretch only go as far as  you can without bending your knee  whole for at least fifteen to thirty  seconds and repeat on the other side be  sure to keep your back flat on the mat  throughout the stretch avoid squat jumps  generally you should not be running or  performing any jump based exercises the  high impact from the movement will only  create more stress on your lower back  which can lead to further injury and  slower recovery if you experience back  pain or discomfort after performing jump  based exercises chances are it is due to  poor posture or a tight muscle so check  your form and take it a notch down as  you strengthen the weak muscles perform  wall squat instead this is a low-impact  workout that does not put any strain on  the lower back yet it is extremely  effective in strengthening your legs  glutes hip flexors and also core simply  find a spot against the wall then stand  about one foot away  lean back until your back is fully flat  against the wall then slide down until  your knees are bent at a 90 degree angle  pressing your lower back into the wall  and hold for about thirty to sixty  seconds as you progress you can perform  basic squat off the wall but still  making sure that your back is flat chest  up and your fully engaging the muscles  in your lower body so stop doing  exercises that can hurt and wasn't  you're already fragile back and start  performing the right and safe exercises  that can actually help you relieve back  pain and strengthen your back and core  to prevent any further injuries or  stiffness aim to perform each exercise  for fifteen to twenty repetitions and a  total of two to three sets perform these  exercises regularly and you will have a  stronger call and it will also increase  your flexibility be sure to LIKE this  video share it on with someone who might  be suffering from lower back pain to  help them through it do also check out  more workout videos &amp; fitness tips on my  channel hit the subscribe button and get  notified when I upload new videos every  week all the best

